The common statute is wound down before one current can use it to expel the
others. Each organisation regains legal autonomy, while a federal council
keeps common lists, finance rules and parliamentary arbitration. Razem ceases
to be a merged current because the party itself has been dissolved—not because
later prose forgot which settlement was chosen.

