new-page: true
on-arrival: merger_resolution = "Razem won membership ballot"; merger_leader = "Razem"; left_dominant_current = "razem"; left_machine_controller = "shared"; left_constitution = "single_leadership_protected_currents"; left_project = "Member-ratified Razem-led Left"; left_party_name = "Lewica Razem"; razem_org_status = "merged_current"; razem_dissent -= 8; razem_strength += 2; barons_dissent += 5; spring_dissent += 2; left_leadership_result = "Razem won the merged party membership"; news_headline = "Razem wins a full membership mandate over the merged Left"

Razem wins not merely among its original members but across the common party.
The result settles the question the apparatus raised: Razem governs because
the merged membership chose it. SLD and Wiosna remain internal currents with
protected rights, not co-owners entitled to treat the winner as a visitor.

