@pps_democratic_split
# prose-audit: Grade C — The politics are right, but the scene talks about its own bookkeeping in front of the player: the subtitle promises that "only seats already tracked as PPS-aligned leave the player's party", and an outcome explains that the split "transfers organisers and legal identity rather than inventing MPs from the general Left total". That is a note to the auditor, printed as prose.
title: PPS asks for an autonomous route
subtitle: A stable democratic merger leaves one small socialist organisation unsure whether it still needs the common party.
new-page: true

= July 2021 — A separate PPS circle?

The merger has survived precisely because its larger currents accepted a
democratic settlement. PPS now argues that this makes an autonomous socialist
organisation possible without bringing the whole Left down with it. We can
keep PPS as an associated current, accept a friendly organisational split or
use party discipline to stop the departure.

- @pps_associate
- @pps_accept_split
- @pps_crush


@pps_associate
title: Keep PPS as an autonomous associated current
subtitle: PPS retains its identity and parliamentary representation inside the common Left.
on-arrival: pps_democratic_split_done = 1; left_revolt_event_done = 1; merger_resolution = "PPS associated current"; pps_active = 1; pps_in_left = 1; pps_org_status = "associated_current"; pps_party_formed = 0; party_unity += 3; pps_dissent -= 7; labor_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "PPS remains an autonomous current inside the common Left"

PPS keeps its name, internal officers and historical rituals while accepting
the common list and leadership rules. No seats move because no organisation
leaves.

